WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.130
Same model. Different harness.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.788
Wildly different agent. So what is the harness?

00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:12.770
A harness is everything around the model that turns text prediction into work done.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:18.012
The loop. The tools. The prompts. The permissions.

00:00:18.562 --> 00:00:23.140
At the core sits a while-loop. Send the conversation to the model.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:27.184
Run the tool calls. Append the results, and go round again.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:31.016
A prompt instruction merely lowers the odds.

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:34.364
A hook blocks a dangerous command every single time.

00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:39.528
Context engineering asks what the model sees at this moment, and why.

00:00:39.628 --> 00:00:47.560
Always in: the system prompt and Claude dot M D. On demand: files and search results.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.714
Never: whole codebases.

00:00:50.264 --> 00:00:56.400
On tools, a tool is three prompts wearing a schema: the name, the description,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.382
and the shape of what comes back.

00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:04.314
That's the agent harnesses handbook. Start with page one: What a Harness Is.
